    "id": 391,
    "chapter": 5,
    "chapterTitle": "Blood Products, Transfusion, and Fluid Therapy",
    "stem": "A 42-year-old woman is anesthetized for resection of a large (22-kg), highly vascular sarcoma in the abdomen. During the resection, 20 units of RBCs, 6 units of platelets, 10 units of cryoprecipitate, 5 units of FFP, and 1 L of albumin are administered. At the conclusion of the operation, the patient’s vital signs are stable, and she is transported to the intensive care unit. Three and a half hours later, a diagnosis of sepsis is made, and antibiotic therapy is started. Which of the items below would be the most likely cause of sepsis in this patient?",
