    "explanation": "A 20-kg, 5-year-old child has an EBV of 70 mL/kg = 1400 mL. The acceptable blood loss can be determined by use of the following formula: maximum allowable blood loss (in mL) = EBV × (Hcts − Hct1)/Hcts where EBV is the estimated blood volume (in mL), Hcts is the starting hematocrit, and Hct1 is the lowest acceptable hematocrit. For this patient, the maximal allowable blood loss = 1400 × (40 - 30/40) = 1400 × (10/40) = 350 mL. This assumes that the patient is getting volume expansion with crystalloid (3 mL per mL of blood loss). Also see explanation to Question 393 (Basics of Anesthesia, ed 7, p 594)."
